  "interpretation": "The host MoE route capture is stale for all-GPU layer-1 rows at positions 511 and 513: it repeats the same-position layer-0 input. The verifier device-side ffn_x shows the actual GPU-profile MoE input equals the CPU-mirror input bitwise across all 16 decode rows. Combined ffn_y matches at 511 and 513; it first differs at 512, matches again at 513, then differs at 514\u2013526. Per-expert parity shows Q8_1 CPU equals CUDA for all tested experts. At 512, expert 90 remains CPU-default in the GPU-profile arm while the experts moved from CPU mirror to GPU have exact Q8_1/CUDA parity. At 514, experts 30, 159 and 182 remain CPU-owned but use default CPU math in the GPU-profile arm instead of Q8_1. This strongly supports CPU activation-format math as the source of those row-level combined-output differences, without proving a complete weighted-sum decomposition or the later persistent-state divergence cause."
